@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@
+# K3 TP3 across three physical DGX Sparks: gated implementation map
+
+This document accompanies the CPU-only `rank_protocol` milestone. It is a design
+and validation contract, **not evidence of CUDA, NCCL, or multi-host execution**.
+
+## Process topology
+
+Run exactly one process and one local CUDA device per Spark:
+
+```text
+global rank 0 / local device 0   coordinator + sampler + full LM head
+global rank 1 / local device 0   worker
+global rank 2 / local device 0   worker
+```
+
+Global rank must never be confused with CUDA ordinal. `ncclCommInitAll({0,1,2})`
+cannot span these hosts; every process sees its own device 0.
+
+## Control-plane sequence
+
+```text
+all ranks -> Hello(model digest, plan digest, exact TP3 shape)
+rank 0    -> ncclGetUniqueId()
+rank 0    -> NcclUniqueId(same opaque 128 bytes to ranks 0/1/2)
+each rank -> ncclCommInitRank(world=3, id, global_rank)
+all ranks -> NcclReady
+rank 0    -> BeginLoad
+each rank -> open local GGUF set; load only its planned rank slice
+all ranks -> LoadReady
+rank 0    -> Token(sequence, token_id)
+all ranks -> one local forward step with distributed NCCL collectives
+all ranks -> StepDone(sequence)
+rank 0    -> sample next token, then broadcast the next Token
+rank 0    -> Finish(next sequence) after EOS
+all ranks -> FinishAck(next sequence), then close cleanly
+```
+
+Any timeout, protocol violation, CUDA failure, loader failure, NCCL async error, or
+forward failure is sticky. Rank 0 broadcasts `Abort`; the control thread on every
+host must call `ncclCommAbort` before joining the compute thread. Continuing after
+one rank leaves a collective is forbidden because the remaining ranks can block or
+consume partial state indefinitely.
+
+CRC32 detects accidental frame corruption. It is not authentication. The transport
+must bind each connection to exactly one configured global rank (or a mutually
+authenticated certificate identity), reject duplicate live rank connections, and
+pass a nonzero, connection-stable `AuthenticatedPeer` to `Coordinator::accept`.
+The coordinator rejects any rank mismatch with the in-band `Message::rank`, any
+unset connection id, and any second connection id for an already bound rank;
+callers must never derive this identity from the message body. Use a private cluster
+network or mutually authenticated TLS if peers are not fully trusted.
+
+The fixed header is 16 bytes and the payload is bounded to 250..506 bytes
+(`kMaxFrameBytes == 522`). A transport must reject a declared payload outside that
+range before allocating a receive buffer or reading the body.
+
+## Exact implementation map
+
+| File / symbol | Required next change | Gate before proceeding |
+|---|---|---|
+| `runtime/include/sparkinfer/tp/collective.h` | Add a distinct one-rank-per-process collective API with in-place `allreduce_f32`, async-error query, and `abort`. Do not overload the existing group-vector contract. | CPU interface test; default local collective unchanged. |
+| `runtime/src/tp/collective.cpp` / `NcclCollective::create` | Leave `ncclCommInitAll` intact for one-host TP. Add `NcclRankCollective::create(world, rank, local_device, id)` using `ncclCommInitRank`. Add `static_assert(sizeof(ncclUniqueId) == dist::kNcclUniqueIdBytes)`. | Three-process NCCL microtest: repeated f32 sums, timeout, deliberate rank abort. No model. |
+| New `runtime/include/sparkinfer/tp/rank_transport.h` and `runtime/src/tp/rank_transport_tcp.cpp` | Blocking framed send/receive around `encode_message`/`decode_message`, reject headers above `kMaxFrameBytes` before body allocation, connection and phase deadlines, one authenticated/configured connection per rank, and a dedicated control thread able to deliver Abort while compute is blocked. | Three localhost processes complete bootstrap, two token steps, clean Finish/FinishAck, rank-spoof, duplicate-connection, disconnect, timeout, and corrupt/oversize-frame tests. |
+| `runtime/include/sparkinfer/models/kimi_k3_tp.h` | Add a separate `KimiK3DistributedRank` holding one `KimiK3TPRank`, one local stream, one rank collective, and `RankSession`. Do not put remote ranks into `KimiK3TP::ranks`. | Compile-only with TP off; ownership/free tests. |
+| `runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_tp.cpp` / `kimi_k3_tp_init` | Preserve the existing local TP path. Add `kimi_k3_dist_rank_init` instead of weakening the current guard globally. Validate the exact rank spec and homogeneous supported expert qtypes, then call `moe_all_expert_width_dims(896,1536,3,rank,256,...)`. | Each rank logs `[0,896)` experts and FFN bands `[0,512)`, `[512,1024)`, `[1024,1536)`; any drift is fatal. |
+| `runtime/src/models/kimi_k3.cpp` / `k3_moe_ffn_local` | Honor `MoeShardMode::AllExpertsFfnWidth`, returning 512. Today it only recognizes `shard.moe_2d`. | Scratch and weight strides agree at 512 in decode and prefill tests. |
+| `runtime/src/models/kimi_k3.cpp` / `upload_sliced` | Reuse the planner-produced `ExpertRow2D` gate/up copies and `ExpertCol2D` down copy. Keep all 896 expert identities. Do not invent offsets in the loader. | Per-rank byte hashes of small synthetic expert tensors match CPU plan; real release triplets pass the fail-closed quant contract. |
+| `runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_tp.cpp` / `kimi_k3_tp_forward_token` | Extract a rank-local eager forward: embed; Attn; optional per-rank NCCL reduce; FfnPartial; per-rank NCCL reduce; FfnFinish; swap. Remove `issue_all` and group-vector reductions only in the new distributed path. | One synthetic layer vs TP1, then one full eager token vs TP1. `SPARKINFER_K3_MOE_WEPS=0`. |
+| Same forward, graph code | Disable CUDA graph capture initially. Cross-process NCCL graph capture is a later optimization, not a bring-up dependency. | Eager parity established before any capture experiment. |
+| Same forward, head block | For the first correct implementation, keep a full output head on rank 0 and skip it on ranks 1/2. Rank 0 samples, then broadcasts the next token. Do not attempt the existing local multi-device logit-band gather across hosts. | Full logits on rank 0 match TP1 within the agreed float32 reduction tolerance. |
+| New `runtime/examples/kimi_k3_dist_generate.cpp` | CLI for `--rank`, `--world-size 3`, `--coordinator`, `--local-device 0`, manifest digest, and timeouts. Rank 0 alone tokenizes/samples/prints. | Identical prompt/token sequence logged by all ranks; rank 1/2 never sample. |
+| `runtime/CMakeLists.txt`, `runtime/tests/CMakeLists.txt` | Keep `rank_protocol` CPU-only and unconditional; compile TCP and NCCL adapters behind explicit options. | Normal TP-off CPU CI stays green. |
+
+## Model and plan identity
+
+Do not hash 330 GB at every launch. Distribute a signed/canonical manifest containing
+the nine shard names, sizes, and precomputed SHA-256 values. `model_digest` is the
+SHA-256 of that canonical manifest. `plan_digest` is the SHA-256 of the exact runtime
+base/patch identifiers plus the tensor-role/qtype contract and these fixed values:
+
+```text
+world=3, experts=896, moe_ffn=1536, block=256
+rank0 ffn=[0,512), rank1=[512,1024), rank2=[1024,1536)
+gate/up split ne1; down split ne0; WEPS=0
+```
+
+Every message repeats both digests. A mismatch aborts before NCCL initialization or
+model loading.
+
+## Why the first head must be rank-0-only
+
+The current one-host path bands the vocabulary and copies all logit bands into one
+host buffer. Across physical Sparks that becomes a new variable-size gather because
+`163840 % 3 != 0`. For the correctness milestone, retain the full output head only
+on rank 0. All ranks already hold the same post-reduce hidden state. This avoids a
+second distributed protocol and keeps temperature-0.2 sampling exact. Optimize the
+head only after end-to-end parity.
+
+## Validation ladder
+
+1. CPU protocol test in this patch.
+2. Three localhost processes using the future TCP adapter; no CUDA.
+3. Three Sparks running only a repeated NCCL f32 all-reduce microtest.
+4. Synthetic expert layer with 896 identities and 512-wide local bands.
+5. One full eager token, approximation off, versus TP1 logits.
+6. Multiple depths including a real long prompt; report KLD, top-1 agreement, RMS
+   delta-probability, and generated-token identity.
+7. Only then benchmark tokens/s and consider graph capture or head sharding.
+
+## Futile or unsafe shortcuts
+
+- `ncclCommInitAll` with device ordinals 0/1/2 across machines.
+- Putting remote Sparks into the existing `KimiK3TP::ranks` vector.
+- Calling group-vector collectives with one local buffer and pretending missing
+  remote buffers are local.
+- Removing only the `896 % 3` guard without the 512-width executor change.
+- Treating gate/up/down as one generic column shard.
+- Enabling peer-one-shot or NVSwitch multimem across separate Sparks.
+- Benchmarking with `SPARKINFER_K3_MOE_WEPS` enabled before long-context parity.
+- Adding FlashKDA, speculative decoding, or vLLM code to this bring-up path; none
+  solves the one-rank-per-process state/collective contract.
